<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phra Mueang Kaeo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1495">1495</a>–<a href="/years/1525">1525</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Phaya Kaeo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phra Mueang Kaeo was a king of Lan Na from 1495 to 1525, the last strong ruler of its golden age. He built and restored many temples, fought wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a>, and patronised Pali scholarship; the chronicle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jinakalamali">Jinakalamali</a> was completed during his reign. After his death Lan Na entered a period of court factionalism that ended in Burmese conquest.</p></div>
